\end{align*}
The pattern here is not immediately clear, but the sum of the series can be calculated by recognizing that it is a sum of squares of odd numbers. The sum of squares of the first $n$ odd numbers is given by $\frac{n(4n^2 - 1)}{3}$. Here, $n = 9$, so the sum of squares is:
\begin{align*}
&= 9 \times \frac{9(4 \times 81 - 1)}{3} \\
&= 9 \times \frac{9 \times 323}{3} \\
