(1 + r \cos \theta + r^2 \cos 2\theta)^2 + (r \sin \theta + r^2 \sin 2\theta)^2 &= 16 \\
1 + 2r(\cos \theta + \cos 2\theta) + 2r^2(\cos^2 \theta + \sin^2 \theta) + r^4 - 8r &= 0.
\end{align*}
This simplifies to
\begin{align*}
r^4 + 9r^2 + 2r \cos \theta - 9r - 7 &= 0.
\end{align*}
By the AM-GM inequality, we have
\begin{align*}
(4r^2 + 5r^2) < 9r^2 + 2r \cos \theta \\
0 < -4r + 5r^2 + r \cos \theta \\
0 < r(5r + \cos \theta) - 4r \\
\sqrt{m}n < 4r \leq 4
\end{align*}
where $m=9$ and $n=3$. Thus, $m+n=\boxed{12}$.

